<title>UK: Swedish green rate to devalue Friday - HGCA.</title>
<headline>Swedish green rate to devalue Friday - HGCA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swedish crown's green rate will be devalued with effect from Friday, the UK's Home Grown Cereals Authority said.</p>
<p>The relative strengths of sterling and the Irish punt mean that the UK and Irish green rates will go into the first of five possible 10-day confirmation periods ahead of a revaluation, which would be on March 29 if their strength is maintained.</p>
<p>Swedens new green rate is 8.69363 to the ecu, compared with the old rate of 8.64446.</p>
<p>Green rates are used by the European Union to convert ecu into the currencies of its member states in its Common Agricultural Policy.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
